# Story 98: Workspaces (##ws) (40s)
# Hook: A workspace is your shared space -- API-key-scoped, and managed right from rysh mode.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-098-workspaces.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
A workspace is your shared space -- API-key-scoped, and managed right from rysh mode.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and double-Escape into rysh mode. Workspaces are managed with the ##ws command.

[00:09.0 --> 00:18.0]
##ws list shows the workspaces you can reach. Each API key is scoped to exactly one workspace, so access stays isolated.

[00:18.0 --> 00:28.0]
##ws create takes a name and an API key, registering a new workspace you can share into.

[00:28.0 --> 00:36.0]
List once more to see it. The new workspace is keyed and ready for shares and subscribers.

[00:36.0 --> 00:40.0]
One API key, one workspace -- clean boundaries for every team you collaborate with.

